// webband_colony — the TROOPS basic strike, one program per raider rank
// (Webband port, slice S5c).
//
// Webband's enemies do not carry catalog specs for their ordinary swing:
// `basicStrike(unit)` (F:\MB\src\battle\engine.ts) deals the unit's own
// TROOPS `dmg`, and only the KITS identities (raider/elite_leader/warlord)
// add catalog abilities on top. The faithful port of a stat-carried swing
// onto a DATA-declared ability catalog is one program per rank carrying
// that rank's number — the engine's `damage` amount is a literal and its
// `scaling_stat_refs` read the built-in `attack_damage` SoA column, which
// this fixture does not seed (rank damage lives in the custom `atk`
// field), so a single scaled program is not expressible today.
//
// TROOPS rows (F:\MB\src\campaign\data.ts:26-46), unchanged from S5's
// hardcoded verb numbers:
//     looter  hp  42  dmg 11  power 1
//     bandit  hp  72  dmg 17  power 2
//     raider  hp 105  dmg 24  power 3.5
//
// Range 2.8 = cleaving_blow's reach — the rank's arm, per S5-prep's KITS
// table (`raider` -> cleaving_blow); the CONE is deliberately not taken
// here (see the fixture header: a rank cone would spray both target
// parities and break the 40-tick per-(tick,target) single-writer
// construction that makes raider damage deterministic; the warlord's
// sweep owns the AoE restoration and pays for it with an exclusive tick
// residue).
//
// Cooldown 2s = 20 ticks = the fixture's `atk_cd` for the ranks (1
// Webband round = 2 s, the S5-prep conversion). The fixture's verb mask
// is what actually gates cadence and reach — these headers are the
// catalog's own statement of the same numbers.
//
// REGISTRY SLOTS. `build_registry` walks the corpus directory
// alphabetically and then each file's declarations in order, so this
// file (t < w) owns ids 1/2/3 in the order below. The fixture seeds
// `ability_id` per rank at spawn and dispatches
// `apply_ability self.ability_id`; `ability_registry_ids_are_pinned` in
// crates/sims/tests/webband_colony.rs asserts the mapping name-by-name
// so a rename or a new file can never silently mis-dispatch.

// AbilityId 1 — looter.
ability WebbandLooterStrike {
    target: enemy, range: 2.8
    cooldown: 2s
    hint: damage

    damage 11
}

// AbilityId 2 — bandit.
ability WebbandBanditStrike {
    target: enemy, range: 2.8
    cooldown: 2s
    hint: damage

    damage 17
}

// AbilityId 3 — raider.
ability WebbandRaiderStrike {
    target: enemy, range: 2.8
    cooldown: 2s
    hint: damage

    damage 24
}
